WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.660
Cats, dogs, and a superpowered guinea pig?

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.490
Dwayne Johnson's latest team-up with Kevin
Hart looks like a wild addition to the DC

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.080
motion picture canon.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.660
You need to watch this before you see "DC
League of Super-Pets."

00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:20.110
"DC League of Super-Pets" has been in development
since at least 2018, when Warner Bros. revealed

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.410
that they hired "LEGO Batman" writer Jared
Stern to write and direct "League of Super-Pets."

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:30.767
The next year, Sam Levine and Patty Hicks
were signed on to work as co-director and producer.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:35.000
The movie received an initial release date
of May 21st, 2021.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.160
Unfortunately, things didn't go as planned.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.680
Though the timing may seem appropriate, the
chances that "DC League of Super-Pets" was

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.050
delayed due to COVID-19 are low.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.060
Warner Bros. decided to delay the film in
May 2019.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.649
Unless the people at Warner Bros. are fortune
tellers, there was probably some other unrevealed

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:55.840
hiccup that prompted the delay.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.260
That hardly matters, because "League of Super-Pets"
now has a release date of July 29th, 2022.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.119
Thanks to the official synopsis of "DC League
of Super-Pets" and its trailers, we've learned

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:08.880
a lot about the plot.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.380
It looks like Superman and the rest of the
Justice League are kidnapped, leaving Krypto

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.619
and his new friends to rescue them.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:20.179
Ace will lead the team of shelter pets, who
have found new powers thanks to a mysterious

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:23.009
surge from an orange kryptonite gem.

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:27.799
Krypto also loses his super-dog powers, leaving
him powerless like his owner.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:32.840
He is just as susceptible to green kryptonite
as Superman, so he'll have to find a way to

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.380
fight alongside his new buddies after being
reduced to just a normal dog.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.490
His positivity and fearlessness keep his mind
strong and will help him lead the new team.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.240
Will they be able to defeat the orange kryptonite-equipped
Lulu?

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.130
You'll have to see the movie for yourself
to find out.

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:54.259
Dwayne Johnson is leading the charge on "DC
League of Super-Pets" as Krypto the Super-Dog.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:59.679
Krypto is the faithful dog of Superman and
first appeared in "Adventure Comics" #210

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:01.270
in 1955.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.659
The family dog in the El household, Krypto
was used as a test subject to send a rocket

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:09.780
to Earth, as Kal-El's parents needed to make
sure they could land a rocket on the planet

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.180
with their son aboard.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:16.040
Unfortunately, Krypto's rocket goes off course,
but the ship eventually rights itself when

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.060
Kal-El lands on Earth and sends off a signal.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:24.626
Just like his owner, Krypto has super strength,
the power of flight, X-ray vision, and freeze breath.

00:02:24.626 --> 00:02:29.540
Unfortunately, he'll be stripped of all these
abilities in the movie, leaving him like every

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.340
other dog on the street.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.739
This marks the second DC project for Johnson
in 2022, who is set to debut as Black Adam

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.829
on October 21st.

00:02:38.829 --> 00:02:44.209
Johnson wrapped his voiceover role in September
2021 and said the animated film would be incredible.

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:47.730
He's also lovingly nicknamed his character
Bark Kent.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:52.326
The former wrestler's production company,
Seven Bucks Production, is also behind the film.

00:02:53.102 --> 00:02:57.980
The Dwayne Johnson-Kevin Hart duo is back,
as the latter joins "DC League of Super-Pets"

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.379
as Ace the Bat-Hound.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.290
Ace is the companion of, you guessed it, Batman.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:07.918
The crime-fighting pup first appeared in "Batman"
#92 in 1955.

00:03:07.918 --> 00:03:13.099
Much like Krypto and the other pet sidekicks
in the cast, Ace debuted in the original DC

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:18.689
Comics but is mostly known for his time in
the animated shorts series "DC Super-Pets!"

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:23.331
In the film, Ace also boasts super-dog strength,
which he appears to have acquired when a lab

00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:28.159
he's being held in is hit with a surge of
energy that comes from orange kryptonite.

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:30.280
"You're super strong."

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.060
"I should be a lot more dead right now, right?"

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.689
When promoting "DC League of Super-Pets" on
his Instagram, Hart said he was excited to

00:03:37.689 --> 00:03:41.590
be back on the big screen with his longtime
colleague Johnson.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:46.629
Before the animated film, the actors starred
in four films together, "Hobbs &amp; Shaw," "Central

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:51.860
Intelligence," "Jumanji: The Next Level,"
and "Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle".

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.739
Johnson revealed in a "DC League of Super-Pets"
featurette that one of his favorite things

00:03:55.739 --> 00:04:00.840
about the film is Krypto and Ace's relationship,
which he says very much mirrors his real-life

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.189
friendship with Hart.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:09.051
"Russian Doll" star Natasha Lyonne stars in
"DC League of Super-Pets" as Merton, the speedster turtle.

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:15.240
Merton McSnurtle first appeared in "Funny
Stuff" #1 but went by the alias of Terrific Whatzit.

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:20.060
The speedy reptile is the companion of the
Earth-508 version of Wally West.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:24.540
Little Merton dresses like a different Flash,
though, inspired by the golden age version

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.310
of the character Jay Garrick.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:30.920
He sports lighting bolts on his boots and
helmet, but the "DC League of Super-Pets"

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.330
film showcases the turtle in just his shell.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:39.160
In the comics, Merton is granted superpowers
as an experiment to see how someone 100% honest

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.160
handles them.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.170
Merton drops his shell when using his powers,
making him look like anything but a turtle,

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.810
which is why the alias Terrific Whatzit was
born.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.930
It doesn't look like Merton will shed his
shell based on what we see in the trailers,

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.640
but anything is possible.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:59.500
Lyonne also revealed Merton has vision problems,
which can cause serious issues for someone so fast.

00:05:00.123 --> 00:05:05.901
Also joining the new animated film is "Rogue
One: A Star Wars Story" actor Diego Luna as Chip.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:12.440
First appearing in "Green Lantern Vol. 2"
#148 in 1982, Ch’p is a member of the Green

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.840
Lantern Corps and even trained alongside Hal
Jordan.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.020
Luna revealed that his version of Chip is
afraid of basically everything, and he has

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:25.270
the annoying tendency to assume that the worst
is going to happen in any situation.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:30.260
Chip is very wary of himself and what he can
do and has a hard time with self-confidence.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.810
He can manifest electricity from his tiny
little paws and is not fully in control of

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.660
his power at the beginning of the film.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.160
It will be up to the rest of the Super-Pets
to guide Chip and help him control his powers

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.523
and believe in himself.

00:05:43.165 --> 00:05:49.000
The last of the Super-Pets is PB, a pig voiced
by "Saturday Night Live" alum Vanessa Bayer.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:53.810
Not every character in "DC League of Super-Pets"
is pulled from the comics, and PB is a brand

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.510
new character, whose initials we're guessing
stand for "pot-bellied."

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:02.710
According to Bayer, PB is obsessed with Wonder
Woman and feels a connection to the superhero.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:08.000
Bayer admires PB for wearing her heart on
her sleeve and being extremely positive.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.460
As with some of the other pets, it looks like
PB obtains her powers from the explosion at

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.360
a lab where she and others are being held
in cages.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.500
Her new power allows her to grow to collosal
size.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.300
PB can grow as tall as buildings, helping
the pets reach new heights, and can even help

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.580
give them a launch.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.910
The friendly pig will be another positive
force within the team, mirroring a lot of

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.780
Krypto's confidence and friendliness.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.730
Much like PB, Lulu is another character who
was created just for the new film.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:40.959
Kate McKinnon plays the villainous Lulu in
the upcoming movie and appears to be the story's antagonist.

00:06:40.959 --> 00:06:46.150
Lulu is a hairless guinea pig who seems to
be some sort of laboratory experiment, evident

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:49.430
in her ear tag, which reads "Lv1U."

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:53.240
Lulu is one powerful rodent who looks to have
telekinetic powers.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:57.300
She wears orange kryptonite around her neck
and sports a cape that seems to be taken from

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.470
a piece of Superman's costume.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.960
Lulu has a team of guinea pigs at her command,
all of whom look like they've been experimented

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.090
on as well.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.220
McKinnon says Lulu is a small creature who
dreams of being something bigger.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:14.370
While her motives are unclear at this moment,
Lulu seems to take a special interest in Superman

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.530
and takes him down with some kryptonite.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.690
The actress is no stranger to voice roles,
playing characters in films like "The Angry

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.550
Birds Movie," "Ferdinand," and "Finding Dory."

00:07:24.301 --> 00:07:28.620
While some of the animals in "DC League of
Super-Pets" will deny that they are actually

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.940
pets, some still have owners or humans they
are loyal to.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.030
Krypto's owner is Superman, who will be voiced
by John Krasinski.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:39.250
"The Office" alum revealed his casting on
Twitter, noting that he always wanted to do

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.520
a team-up movie with Dwayne Johnson.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.470
In the new film, Superman will be in boatloads
of trouble thanks to Lulu, and Krypto will

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:50.200
recruit his new pals to help him rescue the
owner he loves so much.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.920
Voicing Ace's human sidekick is Keanu Reeves
as Batman.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:58.490
Reeves joined the Warner Bros. film a year
ago, but exactly who he was playing was revealed

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.000
much later in the second trailer for the film.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:06.355
Dascha Polanco of "Orange Is the New Black"
fame will also voice the Green Lantern, Jessica Cruz.

00:08:06.437 --> 00:08:10.860
While Lulu is the big bad in the film, there
will also be a human who's not to be trusted

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:15.680
— Marc Maron will voice Lex Luthor, Superman's
long-time nemesis.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.150
Whether Lulu and Lex work together is also
currently unknown.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.000
"Well, well, well.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.960
If it isn't the Justice League."

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.681
While a lot of actors and their roles in "DC
League of Super-Pets" have been revealed to

00:08:27.681 --> 00:08:30.950
the world, there are quite a few characters
who remain a mystery.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:35.990
Attached to the film in voice roles are Thomas
Middleditch, Ben Schwartz, and Jameela Jamil.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:40.310
We'll have to wait and see which heroes these
actors portray as the release date for the

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:41.310
movies gets closer.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:46.400
Several trailers have been released for "DC
League of Super-Pets," two of which put Krypto

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.000
front and center.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.341
The lovable canine is on a quest to save Superman,
who has been rendered powerless thanks to Lulu.

00:08:53.341 --> 00:08:57.970
As mentioned, all the pets except for Krypto
are being held in some type of shelter when

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:03.030
orange kryptonite drops into their room and
grants them all very different powers.

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:07.060
This looks like it might be the same gem that
Lulu wears around her neck, meaning she might

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:12.180
have been granted those powers at the same
time but was able to escape with the kryptonite.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.500
The trailers also introduce a villainous cat
whose name has not been disclosed.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:21.952
This cat can shoot rockets out of its tail
and looks to be a worthy adversary to the Super-Pets.

00:09:21.952 --> 00:09:26.840
A third special trailer specifically focuses
on Batman and Ace and how their partnership

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:27.840
comes to be.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.350
"As a child, my family was taken from me."

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.780
"As a puppy, I was taken from my family."

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:36.270
It looks like the two don't know each other
before the film and connect on their very

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.780
similar pasts.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:41.801
This third trailer also reveals that we will
definitely see the Batmobile in "DC League

00:09:41.801 --> 00:09:47.370
of Super-Pets," and there's also mention of
Alfred, Robin, Commissioner Gordon, and "whoever

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.720
Morgan Freeman played."

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.030
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:55.690
Plus, even more Looper videos about "DC League
of Super-Pets" are coming soon.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:00.375
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

